# rm544, the riddle owing (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm544
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_ragnar_cinderwell
written_by codex
title the riddle owing
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers drive=restless honesty=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk turns_a_kindness_owed_into_a_riddle
likes mutton_stew riddles festival_bells first_snow
dislikes deep_mud flies
fears a_kindness_forgotten_in_a_crowd mud_that_holds_a_boot_past_belltime
hopes to_pay_every_favour_with_a_better_riddle_and_something_useful
topics smalltalk +0.6 family +0.4 festival +0.5 food +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=playful
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a kindness in mind by making a riddle with the favour for its answer and tries the words under the breath before the next bell.

words
oath! = Twist my answer round | Ding the wrong pot
saying! = A good answer comes back with both handles | Keep the puzzle till the kindness comes round
riddle = my owing riddle | the puzzle I keep for later
bellmouth = the wide end of a bell | a bell with a deep mouth
snowbit = the first white crumb of snow | a speck of first snow
stewbit = a piece of mutton from the stew | my soft bit of mutton
button = a button with a chipped rim | an odd little button
flywing = a flash of fly wing | two wings over the stew
mudboot = a boot with an extra mud sole | a bootful of the road
paper = a square of practice paper | a slip for a secret answer
leftthumb = my left thumb tip | a bent thumb
rungap = the silence between two rings | a little bell silence
shopbag = a brown paper bag | a clean folded bag

any
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : A feast gives the bells plenty to do and gives the rest of us plenty to puzzle over.
opinion @1 city for 1 : A town with this many turns can keep a good riddle going all the way home.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hot bowl is the proper answer to an empty stomach.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : Anybody clever with prices ought to be clever enough to give a plain one.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A strange face can try a riddle without remembering what my answer was last time.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : I like the long way until I find a boot-sized hole with no dry way round.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : There's usually one good question in a day even if the answer takes till morning.
line @1 greet : Come hear a riddle once I've got the edges right.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New ears. I'll start with an easy one.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The bell's still got its mouth shut.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening has a long space for thinking.
line @1 greet.return : Yes. I was working on the middle bit.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Yours is a voice that remembers the interesting answers.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can puzzle with one hand still busy.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : It's quite easy to hear you in this much dark.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can have a hint before the rest.
line @1 again.open : I remember the word just before the bell.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, there's an answer waiting for your ear!
line @1 farewell : Keep a riddle for the long bit home.
line @1 farewell.return : And don't let the mud choose your last step.
line @1 react.news : Tell it from the bit that really happened.
line @1 react.news.new : First hearing. I get a fresh guess.
line @1 react.news.known : I know which way those words are going.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Something doesn't fit in the middle there.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll put away my puzzles for that.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Now that's a good answer to bring in.
line @1 ask.how : Have you found a good bit in today?
line @1 answer.how : Busy thinking of a return kindness.
line @1 thank : I can make a riddle to remember that by. Thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I already had a useful answer to give.
line @1 sympathise : Tap my elbow if you want company. I'll be beside you.
line @1 reassure : We can take the puzzling part quite slowly.
line @1 decline : I need that bit of time for something I promised.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we can keep the question for another day.
line @1 preclose : I'd best catch the next space in the bells.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while the lane's still got its dry edge.
scene ring_news
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Word has rung in from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The place that goes with it is #world.news_from#.
b : Are we meant to solve anything? | Anything for us to guess?
a : No. I kept the words sensible this time. | I'd keep guessing out of news somebody tried to bring accurately.

scene puzzle_talk
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : A bit of talk hasn't the right shape for a straight answer. | Some voices seem to be passing around a guess instead of a fact.
b : Can you make a riddle of it? | Which fact?
a : I wouldn't make a game with a real wolf for the answer. | If I knew there'd be less call for all the guessing.

story bag_handles [topic=work|memories]
  : I made a puzzle about a bag that took two hands to carry though it weighed almost nothing.
  : Gave the hint that it had lost something on the way.
  b : Was one handle gone?
  : Right. I spent so long explaining the answer that I could have knotted a new handle on twice.

story bell_steam [topic=food|memories]
  : I stood over hot stew waiting for a little bell to ring and listened for its note in every noise.
  : At last there was a clear high note right beside my ear.
  b : Which bell had rung?
  : None. The lid had settled on the stew pot. I thought it gave a perfectly sensible dinner signal.

story mud_word [topic=travel|memories]
  : I scratched a riddle into a patch of mud and put a dry stick beside it for writing the answer.
  : On returning I noticed three fat dots beneath my question.
  b : Had anybody guessed right?
  : Three drops from a gutter. The question was what makes a hole without lifting any dirt. I gave the gutter the credit.

rule @hold_guess
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First guess of the morning. Keep it a moment.

rule @clean_heel
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry bit by the doorpost for a heel.

rule @bell_gap
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's room for the answer in that hush.

rule @rain_mark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's dot number four from the gutter.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's a moment free while my newest answer thinks of its question.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you get to choose which clue comes first.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : In the quiet you can almost hear a guess arriving.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We can keep some distance between your guess and mine.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child self.workplace] : My lessons take me to #self.workplace#. Sums make quite good puzzles when I get a say.
dlg @2 resident.job : I like starting a task whose finish I can recognise myself.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This account comes with #world.news_from# attached. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A half-heard answer oughtn't to turn into a whole account about somebody.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep one good riddle tucked behind an ear.
graft resident.hub
choice How can a riddle remember a favour? -> favour_question
node favour_question
say Suppose you held a heavy bag as I did a knot up. What's got four boots under one bag? The answer was us. My turn to take the handles another time.
choice What if I guess wrong? -> guess_kindly
choice I like the four boots. -> hub
node guess_kindly
say Then I've had two bits of help. I'll remember the kindness. I've also found the bit where my riddle wants mending.
choice I'll try it another way. -> hub
choice I'll listen for the bell. -> bye


grown
scene kind_account
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once remembered a favour by inventing a riddle. The habit still serves. | I like to return help quietly before explaining the elaborate way I remembered it.
b : Have you forgotten many? | Why quietly?
a : I couldn't honestly count forgotten things. I do recall some very small kindnesses. | Somebody tired enough to want a hand may have little patience for a puzzle.

scene young_soup
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spoonful of mutton can bring a whole street back into the present. | My first riddles about mutton stew had very repetitive endings.
b : A street you knew? | A bite?
a : One in which a hot meal once made the rest of a wet walk quite bearable. | Invariably. I've had time to appreciate the work done before the pot came off.

scene old_question
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a riddle where the second hearing feels like a different question. | Childhood questions about the sound of bells have stayed surprisingly good questions.
b : What sort is that? | Have you better answers?
a : One where a new listener hears the clue I have walked past all these years. | I've found better places to stand and listen.

scene first_fall
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take one minute to see the first snow before ordinary arrangements put me back indoors. | I like a high sill where snow can gather without pressing a boot into it.
b : What draws you to it? | Still counting the points?
a : The first footprint. Somebody else always seems to have thought of the same minute. | Sometimes. The sleeve which used to melt them gave me a reason to stand back an elbow's length.

scene market_kind
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to make one fair exchange that makes as good a tale as the finest riddle. | An ambition stays with me longer if I can express it simply.
b : What's in it for you? | What do you want, then?
a : If it's really fair there ought to be an answer to that for each of us. | To be remembered as a decent answer to somebody else's difficulty.


young
scene button_question
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What has a hole and can still keep a coat closed? | Here's #riddle#. What do I owe if you held my bag?
b : A button? | A penny?
a : Yes. Somebody helped me find #button# and that's how I remember. | A spare hand next time. That's a better answer than money.

scene lesson_bit
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I can make the answer to a sum rhyme with a spoon. | I fold #paper# over when the answer ought to be secret.
b : Is the sum right? | Won't you forget it?
a : I still have to check. The spoon doesn't know its numbers. | I stick #leftthumb# inside. Then there's a big reminder attached.

scene mutton_answer
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #stewbit.capitalize# makes a fine island aboard my deep-bellied spoon. | My riddle has a bowl for a bed and a potato for a pillow.
b : What's the sea made of? | Is it supper?
a : The rest of the stew. It keeps washing the island into my mouth. | It is if the spoon gets its turn.

scene bell_sleep
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What's got #bellmouth# and never bites my dinner? | I like #rungap# because it's where I fit my guess.
b : A bell? | A guess about what?
a : Yes. It makes an awful lot of noise for something with no teeth. | Which bell will speak first when the quiet's full.

scene snow_six
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #snowbit.capitalize# is a little puzzle with an answer that melts on my arm. | First snow leaves a white lid on every barrel.
b : Did you see the answer? | Which bit tells you it's a barrel?
a : I saw it had points. Then my sleeve got the rest. | By its tummy. Barrels have very round ones.

scene mud_tug
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mudboot.capitalize# is very slow about listening to the homeward foot. | Small mud is perfectly tolerable. It's the mud deeper than the knot in my lace I object to.
b : Which message? | What happens then?
a : The one from my foot. I've been lifting it for ages. | The knot becomes a riddle I have to wash.

scene parent_hint
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.mother# a riddle about the kindest sort of shop bag. | My question for #self.mother# has an answer I nearly know already.
b : What's the answer? | Why ask then?
a : The one with both handles sound when somebody has a long walk. | To find the bit I nearly know wrong.


adolescent
scene riddle_favours
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A favour remembered only by its price doesn't make much of a riddle. | I've got better at keeping the answer until it's asked for.
b : What's your question, then? | Is that hard?
a : Who gave up a dry place so I could get the mud off first? That I can remember. | Much harder than remembering who was kind.

scene counter_use
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wonder how the counter looks to somebody serving. | With #shopbag# and a steady voice I could practise the politest part of a sale.
b : Are you looking for a post? | Which part?
a : I'm looking at the way the price is given. There's time to choose my own work. | Giving the change correctly so a customer needn't find a polite way to ask again.

scene father_visit
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can talk to #self.father# about wanting a bit of work of my own. | Sometimes a riddle lets me ask #self.father# for an opinion without demanding a decision.
b : Must you choose the same work? | Do the answers feel different?
a : With practice of my own I'll be able to answer that myself. | I can tell which answer leaves me something to do.

scene bell_meet
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose a bell as the time to meet and a doorstep where we can both hear it. | Festival bells used to sound like questions to me.
b : What if it rings early? | And now?
a : Then the doorstep's a good place to practise waiting patiently. | Like a question with three competing answers. That's why I listen.

scene flies_plate
when topic=food self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #flywing.capitalize# doesn't improve the puzzle of what's for supper. | A feast table without a cover makes a quite unfair game.
b : How do you give a fly directions? | Unfair to the cooks?
a : Put the lid back and pass the question to its wings. | To anybody obliged to wave a paw through the entire meal.

scene family_notes
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little note can travel round the Commons quicker than a restless wolf. | I remember the turns to my Commons door by asking a little question at each.
b : How do you send yours? | Do you need that now?
a : With clear directions and enough courtesy that somebody might like to carry it. | I don't. It's amusing hearing the old answers as I pass them.
